<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Roman Republic (1798–1799)</h1><p class="st-meta">1798 CE – 1799 CE · capital Rome</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A French-sponsored republic proclaimed in Rome in 1798 after Pope Pius VI was deposed and sent into exile.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the French general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathurin-leonard-duphot">Duphot</a> was killed in a riot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in December 1797, French troops under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-alexandre-berthier">Berthier</a> occupied the city. On 15 February 1798 a republic was proclaimed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-forum">Forum</a>, ending the temporal power of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vi">Pope Pius VI</a> was deported and died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valence">Valence</a> in 1799.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic adopted a constitution modelled on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-first-republic">French Directory</a> but using ancient Roman titles, with consuls, a senate and a tribunate. It absorbed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/anconine-republic">Anconine Republic</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tiberina-republic">Tiberina Republic</a>. French commissioners controlled it, heavy levies and confiscations of art and church property caused hardship, and peasant revolts broke out.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In November 1798 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples</a> briefly occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. As the French retreated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1799, Neapolitan troops ended the republic in September, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> was restored under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii">Pius VII</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1798 CE – 1799 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.48%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1798 CE – 1799 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rome</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Repubblica Romana (1798)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=roman-republic-1798-1799" aria-label="Roman Republic (1798–1799) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4984 686 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Roman Republic (1798–1799) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5304 942L5325 887M5304 942L5299 903M5304 942L5304 942M5304 942L5054 728M5304 942L5349 976"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5325 887h0M5299 903h0M5304 942h0M5054 728h0M5349 976h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5304 942h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rome. <a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=roman-republic-1798-1799">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
